#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# airy_ai_zero

#% text
# `airy_ai_zero(k)` gives the `k`-th zero of the Airy function `Ai` (all are negative); `airy_ai_zero(k, x0)` gives the `k`-th zero below `x0`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Numerical values: the sign changes are counted in machine arithmetic, the bracket bisected, and the zero refined by Newton's method at the working precision; exact arguments stay unevaluated and `n` gives the values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
n(airy_ai_zero(1))
#% output
#= -2.338107410459767

#% cell
n(airy_ai_zero(3))
#% output
#= -5.520559828095551

#% cell
n(airy_ai_zero(2, -500))
#% output
#= -500.16973203561264

#% cell
n(airy_ai_zero(1), 25)
#% output
#= -2.3381074104597670384891972524

#% cell
n(airy_ai_zero([1, 2, 3]))
#% output
#= [-2.338107410459767, -4.08794944413097, -5.520559828095551]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `airy_ai`, `bessel_j_zero`
